%I A397443 #58 Aug 24 2026 19:37:22
%S A397443 2,4,6,9,12,15,19,22,26,30,34,38,42,46,51,55,59,64,69,73,78,83,87,92,
%T A397443 97,102,107,112,117,122,127,133,138,143,148,154,159,164,170,175,181,
%U A397443 186,192,197,203,208,214,220,225,231,237,242,248
%N A397443 Least integer such that floor(R(a(n))) = n, where R(x) is the Riemann prime counting function (slightly truncated).
%C A397443 Conjecture: n * (log(n)+log(log(n))-1+((log(log(n))-A)/log(n))) is asymptotic to a(n) if and only if A=2.
%H A397443 Juan Arias de Reyna and Jérémy Toulisse, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1203.5413">The n-th prime asymptotically</a>, arXiv:1203.5413 [math.NT], 2012.
%H A397443 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/LogarithmicIntegral.html">Logarithmic Integral</a>.
%H A397443 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/RiemannPrimeCountingFunction.html">Riemann Prime Counting Function</a>.
%F A397443 Limit_{n->oo} a(n)/prime(n) = 1.
%e A397443 Test for a(1): R(2)=1.045 so a(1)=2 because floor(R(2))=1.
%e A397443 Test for a(2): R(3)=1.857 so 3 is not a term because floor(R(3))<2.
%e A397443 Test for a(2): R(4)=2.336 so a(2)=4 because floor(R(4))=2.
%o A397443 (PARI) a(n) = for(N=2, oo, my(a070769=solve(x=1.4, 2, real(eint1(-log(x)))), RI=sum(M=1, log(N)/log(a070769), (moebius(M)/M)*intnum(T=a070769, N^(1/M), 1/log(T)))); if(floor(RI)==n, return(N)));
%Y A397443 Cf. A000040, A000720, A121046, A070769.
%K A397443 nonn,new
%O A397443 1,1
%A A397443 _Alain Rocchelli_, Aug 08 2026
